Bots filled into an LFG dungeon are teleported to the entrance.
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
         (FillLfgRaidGroup per-add teleport)

Why: report #131 -- "playerbots should automatically be summoned to dungeons
when they join the queue (i can summon them by typing "summon" in party
chat, but i shouldn't have to)".

FillLfgRaidGroup adds idle bots directly to the proposal group, bypassing
the normal queue/rolecheck/teleport flow -- so the bot materialises wherever
it was standing. MakeNewGroup teleports only the players it knows about
(playersToTeleport) and never sees the fill's additions; the player was left
typing "summon" five times per dungeon.

Teleport happens per-add inside the fill loop: dungeon coords come from the
leader's selected dungeons (the group's own dungeon id is not written until
MakeNewGroup finishes, after this hook returns -- GetDungeon(group) reads
empty here). Dead, in-combat or mid-teleport bots are skipped, matching the
refusals TeleportPlayer itself would raise; a dead bot must not be
resurrected into a dungeon for free. RANDOM-dungeon entries whose coords
were filled from areatrigger data at startup teleport to the same entrance
square MakeNewGroup uses.
